    "episode_id": "VR-478073",
    "evidence": "INV-2207's own printed figures do not reconcile. Each line total is arithmetically correct (6 x 24.50 = 147.00; 200 x 0.45 = 90.00; 2 x 38.00 = 76.00; 3 x 12.80 = 38.40; 1 x 15.00 = 15.00), but those five line totals sum to 366.40, not the 376.40 printed as the subtotal - an overstatement of 10.00. The VAT and total are then derived consistently from the inflated subtotal (20% of 376.40 = 75.28; 376.40 + 75.28 = 451.68), so the error propagates: the sum of the line items plus 20% VAT is 366.40 x 1.20 = 439.68, which is 12.00 less than the 451.68 total due.\n\nThe claim under review is therefore false as stated: 451.68 is not the sum of the line items plus 20% VAT. I note the honest uncertainty that the printed table may omit a line (a 10.00 charge would close the gap), but no such line appears on the invoice, and on the document as issued the stated total does not equal its line items plus VAT.",
